sible text source files for a literal string.\n\n    Args:\n        query: query\n        paths: paths\n        limit: limit\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_range(path: string, start_line: integer, end_line: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read an inclusive line range from a text file. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        start_line: start line\n        end_line: end line\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_symbol(path: string, symbol: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a complete Python class or function including decorators. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        symbol: symbol\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_file(path: string, content: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        content: content\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef replace_text_batch(path: string, edits: array, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Atomically replace unique nonoverlapping occurrences from one file version. Returns ok, path, before_hash, file_hash, changed.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        edits: Python list of objects, e.g. [{'old_text':'before','new_text':'after'}]; all refer to the original file.\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..3000 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Optional stable note key; source notes still allow 20..3000 characters.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nComplete the requested local task.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"source\", \"editable\": [], \"required_full_reads\": [], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 8}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline 